  "notes": "USAGE: {結局|けっきょく} summarizes a situation by stating the final outcome, often after various attempts or considerations. It can carry a nuance of \"despite everything\" or resignation.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {結局|けっきょく}のところ (after all, in the final analysis)\n- {結局|けっきょく}は (in the end)\n\nPOSITION: Usually placed at the beginning of a clause or sentence.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {結局|けっきょく} - in the end (summarizing final result)\n- {最後|さいご}に - lastly, finally (sequence)\n- ⟦{結果|けっか}→結果：02486_kekka⟧ - result (noun, not adverb)",
